WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.820
Stick to the trail.

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.060
This goddamn weather.

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:05.500
Been two days or more like this now.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.700
Oh, it has to blow over soon.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.700
Careful over this bridge here.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.260
I can't believe we lost Davey, too.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.660
He's the last one, Arthur.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:38.240
No more.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:41.900
We need to get those people warm and fed.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.240
At least we don't need to worry about Pinkerton's tailing us in this.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:48.120
A couple more days.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:50.560
We'll be on the other side.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.320
You need to help me pick the others back up.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:59.900
You're the only one I can rely on to stay strong right now.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.420
We got fire and shelter.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:03.780
That's a start.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:08.460
Get a move on, Arthur.

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:11.440
There you are.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:12.940
Just stay close.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.520
So, do you think it was a trap in Blackwater?

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:22.140
That many men?

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.020
They knew we were coming.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.840
There was money on that boat, all right.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.060
Lots of it.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:34.520
I stashed what we took with all our money in town right before we fled.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:39.000
Wait.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.120
Is that someone coming towards us?

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:53.640
You up ahead.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:54.740
Who's there?

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:56.340
Whoa.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:01.060
Micah.

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:03.920
Gentlemen.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.400
Found anything?

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.120
I think so.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.480
Found a little homestead down that way.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:10.900
Okay.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.100
Anyone home?

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:13.680
Sure.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.080
Place is blazing with light and noise.

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:17.620
Sounded like a party.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:18.560
Let's go see.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:19.560
Follow me.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.440
How's Davey doing?

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:22.660
He didn't make it.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.200
Nor did little Jenny.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:26.120
That's too bad.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:27.900
Davey was a real fighter.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.900
Both of them calendar boys is.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:31.900
Or was.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:32.900
Yeah.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:34.900
And Mac, Sean?

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:35.900
We don't know.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:37.900
Quite a business.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:43.900
I'm glad you're all right, Micah.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:45.900
Always.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:47.900
Ask him if he's seen John.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:51.900
Hey, have you seen John, Micah?

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.900
Didn't see much of anything once this storm came in.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:56.900
He hasn't seen anything.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:57.800
He hasn't seen anything.

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:58.800
You're going to have to wait until you see him.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:02:59.800
He'll be fine.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.800
Things always turn out right for that boy.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.800
I hope Mac and Sean are still out there somewhere, too.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:10.800
Hey, Arthur, let me take the rear.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:11.800
You move up.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:24.800
Are you sure about this, Micah?

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:25.800
Mr. Morgan.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:26.800
I never thought I would be able to do this.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:30.800
I never thought I would be so pleased to see your face.

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:33.800
Been kind of lonely out here.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.800
Where's everyone else?

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.800
Old mining camp back up to hell.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:38.800
Goddamn.

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:44.800
Cuddled around a fire waiting for Daddy to put food on the table.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:49.800
Said it before, we got too many mouths to feed.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.800
Well, we got a few less now, so you should be happy.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.800
That ain't fair, Arthur.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.800
I earned my share.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:00.800
Okay, let's keep it down now, gentlemen.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.800
It's just up ahead.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.800
Snuff and stash those lanterns, boys.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:08.800
Best you two lie low on this.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:12.800
Hey!

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:15.800
Okay, let's head down there.

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:16.800
Hey!

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:17.800
Hey!

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:18.800
Hey!

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:19.800
Hey!

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:20.800
Hey!

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:21.800
Hey!

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:22.800
Hey!

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:23.800
Hey!

